1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,000
When a signed medical-device requirement changes—say an infusion limit
moves from 5.0 to 5.5 mL/hr—

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,500
teams must prove which hazards, Jira work, tests,
and approvals are affected.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:20,000
MedTrace tracks that chain on live Atlassian data, revokes stale approvals,
enforces the gate, and creates linked re-verification tasks.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:28,000
LIVE mode starts fail-closed with zero hazards.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:39,000
One click on Sync Live Atlassian ingests real Jira issues,
Confluence remote links, and native issue links—

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:50,000
with no fabricated risk metrics.

7
00:00:50,500 --> 00:01:02,000
Recording passing test evidence and signing the Confluence spec's
SHA-256 hash satisfies the release gate—

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:16,000
so the real Jira workflow validator allows moving this compliant issue
from Under Review to Done.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Now SRS-201 changes from 5.0 to 5.5.

10
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The Confluence trigger recomputes the hash, revokes the stale signature
automatically, and traces the complete transitive blast radius.

11
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:24,000
With approval drifted or evidence missing, the same Jira workflow validator
blocks the transition to Done—

12
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:39,000
contrasted directly with our compliant issue.

13
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Through hosted Atlassian MCP over OAuth, verify-iec-compliance flags the drift,

14
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:18,000
and create-reverification-task creates and links the Jira follow-up task—
invoked by the user, never silently auto-created.

15
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:35,000
The Jira issue link and hash-chained audit record close the loop.

16
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:50,000
A Confluence requirement changes; MedTrace proves the impact, revokes stale approvals,
and creates linked re-verification work without leaving Atlassian.
